{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat src/jolt/dao/stream/ws/tcp.jolt'","aggregated_output":"(ns dao.stream.ws.tcp\n  \"Jolt-only TCP substrate under the native WebSocket host adapter (J6d,\n   plan v2 §3; docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md §9.3): nonblocking\n   stream sockets over `jolt.socket.native`, never the `jolt.socket` java.net\n   shim, whose write path waits for the socket to drain.\n\n   Every descriptor made here is nonblocking and close-on-exec, and carries\n   SIGPIPE suppression (SO_NOSIGPIPE on macOS from `new-socket` and\n   `guard-accepted!`, MSG_NOSIGNAL per send on Linux), so a write to a peer\n   that has gone answers an error instead of ending the process. An accepted\n   descriptor is made nonblocking explicitly: Linux does not inherit the\n   listener's mode.\n\n   Nothing here waits. Connect answers `:connecting` on EINPROGRESS and\n   `connect-result` reads SO_ERROR once the descriptor is writable; recv and\n   send are one transfer each (EINTR retried) answering data, never throwing\n   for a socket condition. End of stream, reset and broken pipe are distinct\n   classes.\n\n   Names: `parse-address` accepts IPv4 and IPv6 literals and `localhost`\n   (mapped to 127.0.0.1) and never calls the resolver (plan v2 A6); any\n   other host is `{:error :host-name-unsupported}`.\"\n  (:require\n    [clojure.string :as str]\n    [jolt.ffi :as ffi]\n    [jolt.socket.native :as native]))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Addresses (plan v2 A6)\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- literal\n  \"{:family :ip} for the numeric literal `s`, the ip in its canonical\n   presentation form, or nil. inet_pton only; no resolver.\"\n  [s]\n  (some (fn [family]\n          (when-let [[sa _] (native/make-sockaddr family s 0)]\n            (try {:family family, :ip (native/sockaddr-ip sa)}\n                 (finally (ffi/free sa)))))\n        [native/af-inet native/af-inet6]))\n\n\n(defn- literal-shaped?\n  \"Whether `s` reads as an attempted address literal rather than a name:\n   only digits and dots, or any colon.\"\n  [s]\n  (boolean (or (str/includes? s \":\") (re-matches #\"[0-9.]+\" s))))\n\n\n(defn parse-address\n  \"`{:family :ip :port}` for `host` and `port`, or `{:error kind}` with kind\n   `:host-name-unsupported` (a name other than localhost), `:malformed-address`\n   (a literal inet_pton refuses) or `:invalid-port`. A bracketed IPv6 literal\n   (`[::1]`) is accepted. Never resolves: names are decidable here and now.\"\n  [host port]\n  (let [h (when (string? host)\n            (if (and (str/starts-with? host \"[\") (str/ends-with? host \"]\"))\n              (subs host 1 (dec (count host)))\n              host))]\n    (cond\n      (not (and (int? port) (<= 0 port 65535))) {:error :invalid-port}\n      (or (nil? h) (str/blank? h)) {:error :malformed-address}\n      (= \"localhost\" (str/lower-case h)) {:family native/af-inet, :ip \"127.0.0.1\", :port port}\n      :else (if-let [lit (literal h)]\n              (assoc lit :port port)\n              {:error (if (literal-shaped? h) :malformed-address :host-name-unsupported)}))))\n\n\n(defn- with-sockaddr\n  \"(f sa len) over a fresh sockaddr for a parsed address, freed after.\"\n  [{:keys [family ip port]} f]\n  (let [[sa len] (native/make-sockaddr family ip port)]\n    (try (f sa len) (finally (ffi/free sa)))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Error classes\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn error-class\n  \"The class of socket error `e`: :reset, :broken-pipe, :refused,\n   :not-connected or :other. A reset and a broken pipe are both a peer that\n   has gone; they stay distinct for diagnostics.\"\n  [e]\n  (cond\n    (= e native/econnreset) :reset\n    (and native/epipe (= e native/epipe)) :broken-pipe\n    (= e native/econnrefused) :refused\n    (= e native/enotconn) :not-connected\n    :else :other))\n\n\n(defn- failure\n  [kind e]\n  {:error kind, :class (error-class e), :errno e, :message (native/error-message e)})\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Descriptors\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn close!\n  \"Close `fd` once. EINTR is not retried: on Linux the descriptor is released\n   whatever close answers, and a retry could close a reused number.\"\n  [fd]\n  (native/c-close fd)\n  nil)\n\n\n(defn shutdown!\n  \"shutdown(2) `fd` for :read, :write or :both; answers nil, ignoring\n   ENOTCONN (a peer that already went).\"\n  [fd how]\n  (native/c-shutdown fd (case how :read native/shut-rd :write native/shut-wr native/shut-rdwr))\n  nil)\n\n\n(defn- nonblocking!\n  \"O_NONBLOCK on `fd`; answers nil or the errno it failed with.\"\n  [fd]\n  (let [[r e] (native/set-blocking! fd false)]\n    (when (neg? r) e)))\n\n\n(defn- open-socket\n  \"A fresh nonblocking, close-on-exec stream socket of `family`, or a\n   failure map.\"\n  [family]\n  (let [fd (try (native/new-socket family) (catch Throwable _ nil))]\n    (if (nil? fd)\n      {:error :socket-failed}\n      (if-let [e (nonblocking! fd)]\n        (do (close! fd) (failure :socket-failed e))\n        {:fd fd}))))\n\n\n(defn local-port\n  \"The port `fd` is bound to (the kernel's pick after port 0), or -1.\"\n  [fd]\n  (native/local-port fd))\n\n\n(defn nonblocking?\n  \"Whether `fd` has O_NONBLOCK set, read back with F_GETFL.\"\n  [fd]\n  (let [[flags _] (native/c-fcntl fd 3 0)]\n    (and (not (neg? flags))\n         (pos? (bit-and flags (if (= native/os :macos) 0x4 0x800))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Listener\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn listen!\n  \"A nonblocking listener on the parsed `addr` (`parse-address`):\n   `{:fd :port}` with the actual port, or a failure map (`:error`\n   `:bind-failed`/`:listen-failed`/`:socket-failed`). The descriptor is\n   closed on failure.\"\n  ([addr] (listen! addr 128))\n  ([addr backlog]\n   (let [{:keys [fd] :as opened} (open-socket (:family addr))]\n     (if-not fd\n       opened\n       (let [_ (native/set-listener-reuse! fd)\n             [rb eb] (with-sockaddr addr (fn [sa len] (native/c-bind fd sa len)))]\n         (if (neg? rb)\n           (do (close! fd) (failure :bind-failed eb))\n           (let [[rl el] (native/c-listen fd backlog)]\n             (if (neg? rl)\n               (do (close! fd) (failure :listen-failed el))\n               {:fd fd, :port (local-port fd)}))))))))\n\n\n;; One accept(2) each; the test seam (redefined by the probe only).\n(defn accept-once\n  [lfd sa lenp]\n  (native/c-accept lfd sa lenp))\n\n\n(defn accept!\n  \"One nonblocking accept on listener `lfd`: `{:fd :peer}` for a connection,\n   explicitly nonblocking, close-on-exec, SIGPIPE-suppressed and\n   TCP_NODELAY; `:would-block` when none is pending; or a failure map\n   (`:error :accept-failed`). EINTR is retried.\"\n  [lfd]\n  (let [[sa lenp] (native/alloc-sockaddr)]\n    (try\n      (loop []\n        (let [[fd e] (accept-once lfd sa lenp)]\n          (cond\n            (not (neg? fd))\n            (if-let [e (nonblocking! fd)]\n              (do (close! fd) (failure :accept-failed e))\n              (do (native/guard-accepted! fd)\n                  (native/set-int-option! fd native/ipproto-tcp native/tcp-nodelay 1)\n                  {:fd fd\n                   :peer {:family (native/sockaddr-family sa)\n                          :ip (native/sockaddr-ip sa)\n                          :port (native/sockaddr-port sa)}}))\n            (native/eintr? e) (recur)\n            (native/eagain? e) :would-block\n            :else (failure :accept-failed e))))\n      (finally (ffi/free sa) (ffi/free lenp)))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Dialer\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn connect!\n  \"Start a nonblocking connect to the parsed `addr`: `{:fd :state\n   :connected}`, `{:fd :state :connecting}` (EINPROGRESS: wait for the\n   descriptor to be writable, then `connect-result`), or a failure map\n   (`:error :connect-failed`), the descriptor closed. Never waits.\"\n  [addr]\n  (let [{:keys [fd] :as opened} (open-socket (:family addr))]\n    (if-not fd\n      opened\n      (let [[r e] (with-sockaddr addr (fn [sa len] (native/c-connect fd sa len)))]\n        (native/set-int-option! fd native/ipproto-tcp native/tcp-nodelay 1)\n        (cond\n          (not (neg? r)) {:fd fd, :state :connected}\n          ;; an interrupted connect carries on asynchronously, as EINPROGRESS\n          (or (native/connect-pending? e) (native/eintr? e)) {:fd fd, :state :connecting}\n          :else (do (close! fd) (failure :connect-failed e)))))))\n\n\n(defn connect-result\n  \"The outcome of a connect that answered `:connecting`, read once its\n   descriptor is writable: `:connected` or a failure map (`:error\n   :connect-failed`, from SO_ERROR). Does not close the descriptor.\"\n  [fd]\n  (let [e (native/pending-error fd)]\n    (cond\n      (zero? e) :connected\n      (neg? e) {:error :connect-failed, :class :other, :errno -1, :message \"SO_ERROR unreadable\"}\n      :else (failure :connect-failed e))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Transfers\n;; =============================================================================\n\n;; One system call each, answering [result errno]. The chunk functions call\n;; them through these vars, which is the test-only indirection the J6d probe\n;; redefines to script short, EAGAIN and failing transfers. There is no\n;; production fault mode.\n\n(defn recv-once\n  [fd buf n]\n  (native/c-recv fd buf n 0))\n\n\n(defn send-once\n  [fd buf n]\n  (native/c-send fd buf n native/msg-nosignal))\n\n\n(defn recv-chunk!\n  \"One recv of at most `cap` bytes into native `buf`: `{:n n}` (n > 0),\n   `:eof`, `:would-block`, or a failure map (`:error :recv-failed`, `:class`\n   :reset for ECONNRESET). EINTR is retried.\"\n  [fd buf cap]\n  (loop []\n    (let [[n e] (recv-once fd buf cap)]\n      (cond\n        (pos? n) {:n n}\n        (zero? n) :eof\n        (native/eintr? e) (recur)\n        (native/eagain? e) :would-block\n        :else (failure :recv-failed e)))))\n\n\n(defn send-chunk!\n  \"One send of `n` bytes from native `buf`: `{:n accepted}` (possibly short,\n   possibly 0), `:would-block`, or a failure map (`:error :send-failed`,\n   `:class` :broken-pipe or :reset for a peer that has gone). EINTR is\n   retried.\"\n  [fd buf n]\n  (loop []\n    (let [[r e] (send-once fd buf n)]\n      (cond\n        (not (neg? r)) {:n r}\n        (native/eintr? e) (recur)\n        (native/eagain? e) :would-block\n        :else (failure :send-failed e)))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' src/dev/jolt_udp_probe.clj && cat src/dev/jolt_udp_probe.sh\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' src/dev/jolt_udp_probe.clj && cat src/dev/jolt_udp_probe.sh\"","aggregated_output":";; J0b: raw nonblocking SOCK_DGRAM over jolt.ffi on macOS arm64 and Linux x86_64.\n;; Probe only: no datagram/DHT conformance. Run from the repo root with\n;;   bb probe:jolt-udp\n(ns jolt-udp-probe\n  (:require [jolt.ffi :as ffi]\n            [jolt.socket.native :as native]\n            [jolt.io-poller :as poller]\n            [jolt.fibers :as fibers]\n            [clojure.string :as str]))\n\n\n;; -- constants per platform ---------------------------------------------------\n;; The platform is jolt.socket.native/os (:macos, :linux, :windows), the same\n;; selection jolt's socket layer and sockaddr helpers use; os.name is never\n;; read here (jolt's System/getProperty shim can answer nil).\n;;\n;; :macos from MacOSX.sdk: sys/socket.h:112,155,156,574; netinet/in.h:121;\n;;   sys/errno.h:96,129-130,137,170.\n;; :linux x86_64 from shiva's headers (asm-generic/errno-base.h, errno.h,\n;;   x86_64-linux-gnu/asm/socket.h, bits/socket.h), checked by the\n;;   orchestrator: EAGAIN = EWOULDBLOCK = 11.\n(def platform native/os)\n\n\n(def consts\n  (case platform\n    :macos {:sock-dgram 2 :ipproto-udp 17 :so-sndbuf 0x1001 :so-rcvbuf 0x1002\n            :msg-trunc 0x10 :eagain 35 :emsgsize 40 :enobufs 55 :ebadf 9}\n    :linux {:sock-dgram 2 :ipproto-udp 17 :so-sndbuf 7 :so-rcvbuf 8\n            :msg-trunc 0x20 :eagain 11 :emsgsize 90 :enobufs 105 :ebadf 9}\n    (throw (ex-info \"J0b probe: unsupported platform\" {:platform platform}))))\n\n\n(def SOCK-DGRAM (:sock-dgram consts))\n(def IPPROTO-UDP (:ipproto-udp consts))\n(def SO-SNDBUF (:so-sndbuf consts))\n(def SO-RCVBUF (:so-rcvbuf consts))\n(def MSG-TRUNC (:msg-trunc consts)) ; not used: N+1 sentinel instead\n(def EAGAIN (:eagain consts))\n(def EMSGSIZE (:emsgsize consts))\n(def ENOBUFS (:enobufs consts))\n(def EBADF (:ebadf consts))\n\n\n;; ssize_t sendto(int, const void*, size_t, int, const struct sockaddr*, socklen_t)\n;; ssize_t recvfrom(int, void*, size_t, int, struct sockaddr*, socklen_t*)\n;; socklen_t is 32-bit unsigned on both (arm/_types.h:117; glibc\n;; __socklen_t is __U32_TYPE). Not :blocking: the fd is\n;; nonblocking, so neither call can park the carrier.\n(ffi/defcfn c-sendto \"sendto\" [:int :pointer :size_t :int :pointer :uint] :ssize_t\n            {:capture-native-error true})\n\n\n(ffi/defcfn c-recvfrom \"recvfrom\" [:int :pointer :size_t :int :pointer :pointer] :ssize_t\n            {:capture-native-error true})\n\n\n;; -- injection seam -------------------------------------------------------------\n;; The probe's sendto goes through this var. Injected runs rebind it and every\n;; observation they produce is tagged :injected, never :natural.\n(def ^:dynamic *sendto* c-sendto)\n\n\n(defn- classify-send-error\n  [e]\n  (cond (or (= e EAGAIN) (= e ENOBUFS)) :would-block\n        (= e EMSGSIZE) :emsgsize\n        :else :error))\n\n\n;; -- raw surface ------------------------------------------------------------------\n(defn udp-open\n  \"A nonblocking, close-on-exec SOCK_DGRAM fd bound to 127.0.0.1:0.\"\n  []\n  (let [[fd e] (native/c-socket native/af-inet SOCK-DGRAM IPPROTO-UDP)]\n    (when (neg? fd) (throw (ex-info \"socket failed\" {:errno e})))\n    (native/close-on-exec! fd)\n    (let [[r e] (native/set-blocking! fd false)]\n      (when (neg? r) (throw (ex-info \"O_NONBLOCK failed\" {:errno e}))))\n    (let [[sa len] (native/make-sockaddr native/af-inet \"127.0.0.1\" 0)]\n      (try\n        (let [[r e] (native/c-bind fd sa len)]\n          (when (neg? r) (throw (ex-info \"bind failed\" {:errno e}))))\n        (finally (ffi/free sa))))\n    fd))\n\n\n(defn send!\n  \"One sendto of the whole byte array to addr ({:ip :port}). Answers\n   {:result :sent :n} | {:result :would-block :errno} | {:result :emsgsize :errno}\n   | {:result :error :errno} | {:result :short-send :n :len}. A short send is an\n   error and is never completed by a second packet.\"\n  [fd ^bytes payload {:keys [ip port]}]\n  (let [len (alength payload)\n        buf (ffi/alloc (max 1 len))\n        [sa salen] (native/make-sockaddr native/af-inet ip port)]\n    (try\n      (when (pos? len) (ffi/write-array buf payload))\n      (let [[n e] (*sendto* fd buf len 0 sa salen)]\n        (cond\n          (neg? n) {:result (classify-send-error e) :errno e}\n          (not= n len) {:result :short-send :n n :len len}\n          :else {:result :sent :n n}))\n      (finally (ffi/free buf) (ffi/free sa)))))\n\n\n(defn recv!\n  \"One recvfrom with a buffer of limit+1 bytes. Answers\n   {:result :packet :bytes :from} | {:result :oversize :received :limit :from}\n   | {:result :would-block :errno} | {:result :error :errno}. A packet longer\n   than limit is an error; its prefix is never returned.\"\n  [fd limit]\n  (let [cap (inc limit)\n        buf (ffi/alloc cap)\n        [sa lenp] (native/alloc-sockaddr)]\n    (try\n      (let [[n e] (c-recvfrom fd buf cap 0 sa lenp)]\n        (cond\n          (neg? n) {:result (if (= e EAGAIN) :would-block :error) :errno e}\n          :else\n          (let [from {:ip (native/sockaddr-ip sa) :port (native/sockaddr-port sa)}]\n            (if (> n limit)\n              {:result :oversize :received n :limit limit :from from}\n              {:result :packet :bytes (if (zero? n) (byte-array 0) (ffi/read-array buf n))\n               :from from}))))\n      (finally (ffi/free buf) (ffi/free sa) (ffi/free lenp)))))\n\n\n(defn local\n  [fd]\n  (native/local-address fd))\n\n\n(defn close!\n  [fd]\n  (poller/cancel! fd)\n  (poller/forget! fd)\n  (native/c-close fd))\n\n\n;; -- harness ------------------------------------------------------------------------\n(def results (atom []))\n\n\n(defn check\n  [item label ok? detail]\n  (swap! results conj {:item item :label label :ok? (boolean ok?) :detail detail})\n  (println (if ok? \"PASS\" \"FAIL\") item label (pr-str detail)))\n\n\n(defn record\n  \"An observation that cannot fail: printed as RECORD, never counted as PASS.\"\n  [item label detail]\n  (swap! results conj {:item item :label label :record? true :detail detail})\n  (println \"RECORD\" item label (pr-str detail)))\n\n\n(defn drain!\n  \"recv! until :would-block; answers the packet count. A :error result is a\n   FAIL and stops the drain instead of looping on it.\"\n  [item fd limit]\n  (loop [n 0]\n    (let [r (recv! fd limit)]\n      (case (:result r)\n        :would-block n\n        :error (do (check item \"drain stopped on recv error\" false r) n)\n        (recur (inc n))))))\n\n\n(defn ->bytes\n  [xs]\n  (byte-array (map unchecked-byte xs)))\n\n\n(defn pattern\n  [n seed]\n  (->bytes (map #(bit-and (+ seed (* 31 %)) 0xff) (range n))))\n\n\n(defn recv-wait\n  \"recv! until a non-would-block result, waiting on the poller between tries.\n   Counts the wakeups. Thread or fiber, whichever the caller is.\"\n  [fd limit]\n  (loop [waits 0]\n    (let [r (recv! fd limit)]\n      (if (= :would-block (:result r))\n        (do (poller/wait-ready fd :read) (recur (inc waits)))\n        (assoc r :waits waits)))))\n\n\n(defn same-bytes?\n  [a b]\n  (= (vec a) (vec b)))\n\n\n;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n;; Item 1: bind, readback, whole-packet semantics\n(defn item-1\n  [a b N]\n  (let [la (local a) lb (local b)\n        to-b {:ip \"127.0.0.1\" :port (:port lb)}]\n    (check 1 \"bound ports read back\" (and (pos? (:port la)) (pos? (:port lb))\n                                          (not= (:port la) (:port lb)))\n           {:a la :b lb})\n    (check 1 \"empty socket answers :would-block\" (= :would-block (:result (recv! b N)))\n           (recv! b N))\n    (doseq [[label payload] [[\"zero-length\" (byte-array 0)]\n                             [\"embedded-NUL\" (->bytes [0 1 0 0 255 0 65 0])]\n                             [\"limit-sized N\" (pattern N 7)]]]\n      (let [s (send! a payload to-b)\n            r (recv-wait b N)]\n        (check 1 (str label \" round-trip\")\n               (and (= :sent (:result s)) (= (alength payload) (:n s))\n                    (= :packet (:result r)) (same-bytes? payload (:bytes r))\n                    (= (:from r) {:ip \"127.0.0.1\" :port (:port la)}))\n               {:len (alength payload) :send s :recv (dissoc r :bytes)\n                :recv-len (some-> (:bytes r) alength)})))\n    ;; distinct consecutive packets: each receive consumes exactly one\n    (let [ps (mapv #(pattern (+ 10 %) %) (range 5))\n          sends (mapv #(send! a % to-b) ps)\n#!/bin/sh\n# J0b probe runner (foreground), macOS arm64 and Linux x86_64. POSIX sh\n# (Ubuntu's /bin/sh is dash). Run from the repository root.\n#\n#   JOLT       jolt binary. Default: build/tools/jolt/bin/jolt (J0a layout),\n#              else build/jolt-spike/jolt/bin/jolt (spike layout).\n#   JOLT_CHEZ  threaded Chez 10.x. Default: build/tools/jolt-env.sh's value when\n#              that file exists (J0a layout), else the mise 10.4.1 install path\n#              when present; otherwise left unset and jolt searches PATH.\ndir=$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\" && pwd)\n\nif [ -z \"$JOLT_CHEZ\" ] && [ -f build/tools/jolt-env.sh ]; then\n  . build/tools/jolt-env.sh\nfi\nif [ -z \"$JOLT\" ]; then\n  if [ -x build/tools/jolt/bin/jolt ]; then\n    JOLT=build/tools/jolt/bin/jolt\n  else\n    JOLT=build/jolt-spike/jolt/bin/jolt\n  fi\nfi\nif [ -z \"$JOLT_CHEZ\" ]; then\n  mise_chez=\"$HOME/.local/share/mise/installs/chezscheme/10.4.1/bin/scheme\"\n  [ -x \"$mise_chez\" ] && JOLT_CHEZ=$mise_chez\nfi\n[ -n \"$JOLT_CHEZ\" ] && export JOLT_CHEZ\n\njolt_home=$(cd \"$(dirname \"$JOLT\")/..\" 2>/dev/null && pwd)\necho \"jolt: $JOLT\"\necho \"jolt-sha: $(git -C \"$jolt_home\" rev-parse HEAD 2>/dev/null) dirty=$(git -C \"$jolt_home\" status --porcelain 2>/dev/null | wc -l | tr -d ' ')\"\nif [ -n \"$JOLT_CHEZ\" ]; then\n  echo \"chez: $JOLT_CHEZ $(\"$JOLT_CHEZ\" --version 2>&1)\"\nelse\n  echo \"chez: JOLT_CHEZ unset (jolt searches PATH)\"\nfi\n\ncase \"$(uname -s)\" in\n  Darwin)\n    echo \"uname: $(uname -sm) macOS $(sw_vers -productVersion 2>/dev/null)\"\n    echo \"sysctl: $(sysctl -n net.inet.udp.maxdgram net.inet.udp.recvspace kern.ipc.maxsockbuf 2>/dev/null | tr '\\n' ' ')(maxdgram recvspace maxsockbuf)\"\n    echo \"lo0 mtu: $(ifconfig lo0 2>/dev/null | sed -n 's/.*mtu \\([0-9]*\\).*/\\1/p' | head -1)\"\n    ;;\n  Linux)\n    os=$(sed -n 's/^PRETTY_NAME=\"\\(.*\\)\"$/\\1/p' /etc/os-release 2>/dev/null)\n    echo \"uname: $(uname -sm) $os\"\n    sys=\"\"\n    for k in core/wmem_default core/wmem_max core/rmem_default core/rmem_max ipv4/udp_wmem_min ipv4/udp_rmem_min ipv4/udp_mem; do\n      sys=\"$sys net.$(echo $k | tr / .)=$(tr '\\t' ' ' < /proc/sys/net/$k 2>/dev/null)\"\n    done\n    echo \"sysctl:$sys\"\n    echo \"lo mtu: $(cat /sys/class/net/lo/mtu 2>/dev/null)\"\n    ;;\n  *)\n    echo \"uname: $(uname -sm) (unsupported platform for this probe)\"\n    ;;\nesac\n\n\"$JOLT\" \"$dir/jolt_udp_probe.clj\"\nrc=$?\necho \"exit: $rc\"\nexit $rc\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"agent_message","text":"The main gap is the datagram adapter and its DHT wiring: storage, Ed25519 signing, clocks, and the J6 TCP substrate already exist. The UDP design must preserve packet boundaries and report send failures immediately; the TCP pump’s queue and EOF behavior cannot carry over."}}
